This patient has progressive myopia (nearsightedness). There are options to slow how quickly it is worsening during the growing years.\
\
The goal of myopia control is not to reverse nearsightedness, but to slow the rate at which the eye becomes more myopic over time. Slowing progression matters because higher myopia is associated with greater lifetime risk of retinal and other eye problems.\
